# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 Optimization level {#21-optimization-level}"
msgstr "2.1 Antas ng optimization {#21-optimization-level}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`optimization_level` has four options, from 0 to 3. The higher the optimization level, the more computational effort is spent to optimize the circuit. Level 0 performs no optimization and just does the minimal amount of work to make the circuit runnable on the selected backend. Level 3 spends the most amount if effort (and typically runtime) to try to optimize the circuit. Level 1 is the default optimization level.\n"
"We transpile the circuit without optimization (`optimization_level=0`) and with optimization (`optimization_level=2`).\n"
"We see a big difference in the circuit length of transpiled circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `optimization_level` ay may apat na opsyon, mula 0 hanggang 3. Kung mas mataas ang optimization level, mas malaki ang computational effort na ginagastos upang i-optimize ang circuit. Ang level 0 ay walang isinasagawang optimization at ginagawa lang ang minimal na halaga ng trabaho upang gumana ang circuit sa napiling backend. Ang level 3 ay gumagastos ng pinakamalaking effort (at karaniwan ay runtime) upang subukang i-optimize ang circuit. Ang level 1 ang default na optimization level.\n"
"Tina-transpile natin ang circuit nang walang optimization (`optimization_level=0`) at may optimization (`optimization_level=2`).\n"
"Makikita natin ang malaking pagkakaiba sa haba ng circuit ng mga na-transpile na circuit.\n"

